<title>FRANCE: U.S. principal country of origin for Paris Nov 96.</title>
<headline>U.S. principal country of origin for Paris Nov 96.</headline>
<text>
<p>PARIS, Jan 8 (Reuter) The United States was the principal country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in November 1996, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 leading countries of origin for ADP imports in November 1996, with percentage change on November 1995, in parentheses, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	12,417 tonnes  up    4.4pct</p>
<p> 2  Japan		   2,452 tonnes  up   32.9</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong	     2,176 tonnes  up    9.8</p>
<p> 4  United Kingdom	2,122 tonnes  up   89.9</p>
<p> 5  Canada		  2,111 tonnes  down  9.7</p>
<p> 6  India		   1,732 tonnes  down 21.0</p>
<p> 7  Germany		 1,474 tonnes  up   30.3</p>
<p> 8  Thailand		1,220 tonnes  up   38.4</p>
<p> 9  Italy		   1,200 tonnes  up   22.6</p>
<p> 10 Kenya		     802 tonnes  up   20.9</p>
<p> 11 Singapore		 790 tonnes  up   58.8</p>
<p> 12 China		     777 tonnes  up   19.6</p>
<p> 13 Argentina		 668 tonnes  up   21.9</p>
<p> 14 UAE			 596 tonnes  down  3.3</p>
<p> 15 Korea		     589 tonnes  down  7.8</p>
<p> 16 Switzerland	     580 tonnes  up   28.1</p>
<p> 17 Brazil		    509 tonnes  down 21.2</p>
<p> 18 South Africa	    496 tonnes  up   11.0</p>
<p> 19 Cameroon		  476 tonnes  down 24.7</p>
<p> 20 Morocco		   424 tonnes  down 32.5</p>
<p> Total		     33,611 tonnes</p>
<p>Global November 1996 import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 46,976 tonnes, an increase of 10.0 percent on the same month the previous year, ADP said. - Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
